  "releaseNotes": "10.2.0: HelperFunctions.SafeGetSessionData, SafeSetSessionData and SafeRemoveSessionData no longer use thread named data slots (Thread.GetNamedDataSlot / Thread.SetData / Thread.GetData). Reads never consult a thread slot: a read through a null context, or through a live session that lacks the key, returns null; a write or remove without a session is a silent no-op. The HTTP-session path is unchanged when the key is present. Also in 10.2.0: Serializer.SerializeToJson with custom JsonSerializerOptions uses those options as given, so indent: true no longer forces WriteIndented on them (073f040).",
